      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "per sampling step. For autoregressive and block diffusion sampling, generation terminates when the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        265.89337158203125,
        503.9968566894531,
        274.7999267578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "|EOS| token is produced. For block diffusion LLaDA (i.e., semi-autoregressive remasking) and pure",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        276.0850524902344,
        504.0018005371094,
        285.70892333984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "diffusion sampling, the generation length is fixed at 1024 for LLaDA 8B Base, while for LLaDA",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        287.71136474609375,
        504.3633117675781,
        296.617919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "8B Instruct, it is tuned from {64, 256, 512} to balance efficiency and performance. Low-confidence",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        298.620361328125,
        503.99725341796875,
        307.52691650390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "remasking is applied to intra-block diffusion sampling in both block diffusion and block diffusion",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        309.52935791015625,
        503.995361328125,
        318.4359130859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "LLaDA, as well as to pure diffusion sampling. We also test different block lengths for LLaDA 8B",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        320.4383544921875,
        503.99737548828125,
        329.34490966796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Base. For LLaDA 8B Instruct, we only evaluate block length 32 for efficiency, as it yields the best",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        331.34735107421875,
        503.9978332519531,
        340.25390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "results on LLaDA 8B Base.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        342.25634765625,
        218.00698852539062,
        351.16290283203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Additionally, for LLaDA 8B Instruct, due to heavy padding of |EOS| tokens in the SFT data (as",
      "bbox": [
        107.64099884033203,
        357.92803955078125,
        504.00421142578125,
        367.5519104003906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "detailed in Sec. B.1), we observe that under pure diffusion sampling, the proportion of |EOS| tokens",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        368.8370361328125,
        504.0003967285156,
        378.4609069824219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in model outputs becomes very high. This leads to extremely short generations and degrades model",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        380.4633483886719,
        504.0032043457031,
        389.3699035644531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "performance. To mitigate this issue, for HumanEval, MBPP, GSM8K, Math, and GPQA, we set the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        391.3723449707031,
        504.0035095214844,
        400.2789001464844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "confidence score of the |EOS| token to zero during pure diffusion sampling. This adjustment helps",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        401.5640563964844,
        504.0021667480469,
        411.18792724609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "maintain an appropriate ratio of |EOS| tokens during generation.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        412.4730529785156,
        364.9552917480469,
        422.096923828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Finally, we conduct ablation studies to analyze the effects of random and low-confidence remasking",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        429.5793762207031,
        503.99591064453125,
        438.4859313964844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "strategies using the pure diffusion sampling. For efficiency, we use LLaDA 8B Base with generation",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        440.4883728027344,
        503.9983825683594,
        449.3949279785156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "length and sampling steps set to 256 in this analysis.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        451.3973693847656,
        316.6666259765625,
        460.3039245605469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Results. As shown in Tab. 7, for block diffusion sampling, overall performance improves as the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        467.6658020019531,
        503.99737548828125,
        476.6919250488281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "block length increases. Moreover, both Tab. 7 and Tab. 8 show that block diffusion sampling",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        478.6943664550781,
        503.99737548828125,
        487.6009216308594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "consistently outperforms autoregressive sampling, and block diffusion LLaDA sampling further",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        489.6043701171875,
        504.170166015625,
        498.51092529296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "improves upon standard block diffusion sampling. Finally, pure diffusion sampling achieves the best",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        500.51336669921875,
        504.0023193359375,
        509.419921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "overall performance.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        511.42236328125,
        190.68960571289062,
        520.3289184570312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In addition, Tab. 9 shows that the low-confidence remasking strategy consistently outperforms the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        527.8103637695312,
        504.00164794921875,
        536.7169189453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "random remasking strategy. We hypothesize that low-confidence remasking functions similarly to the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        538.7193603515625,
        504.00146484375,
        547.6259155273438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "annealed sampling method used by default in ARMs, improving accuracy by reducing the diversity",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        549.6283569335938,
        504.346923828125,
        558.534912109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of generated sentences.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        560.538330078125,
        200.67213439941406,
        569.4448852539062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We discover that autoregressive sampling leads to very poor performance for LLaDA 8B Instruct.",
      "bbox": [
        107.53199768066406,
        576.9263916015625,
        505.7447814941406,
        585.8329467773438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "This is because each SFT data is a complete sentence, so given a sequence length, LLaDA 8B Instruct",
      "bbox": [
        107.69100189208984,
        587.8353271484375,
        503.9951171875,
        596.7418823242188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tends to generate a full sentence within that length. In contrast, LLaDA 8B Base does not suffer from",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        598.744384765625,
        504.0014953613281,
        607.6509399414062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "this issue, as the pre-training data consists of truncated documents (as detailed in Appendix B.1) and",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        609.6533813476562,
        503.9954833984375,
        618.5599365234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the model is trained with random sequence lengths (as detailed in Sec. 2.2). As a result, when given a",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        620.5623779296875,
        504.0013427734375,
        629.4689331054688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "short sequence length, LLaDA 8B Base tends to generate only part of a sentence, which can then be",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        631.4723510742188,
        503.9959411621094,
        640.37890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
